{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For he says, 'This is it.'</b> And similarly when the defendant who is being sued says, 'This is indeed the truth,' and not your other claims — this is one who admits to part of the claim." "<b>Unto Elohim shall the word of both of them come.</b> The claimant and the defendant, to take an oath — whether they are depositor and bailee, or lender and borrower who admits to part of the claim." "<b>Whom Elohim shall condemn, he shall pay double.</b> But one whom Elohim condemns for theft — because he falsely claimed the defense of theft — he shall pay double, according to the law of a thief."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:46.279052623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}